    {
      "severity": "moderate",
      "description": "Llama4 Libby is discarding to hand size and chose to discard Sire of Seven Deaths, a powerful 7/7 with first strike, vigilance, menace, trample, reach, lifelink, and ward-pay 7 life. With Ugin's Labyrinth and Talisman of Impulse on board (providing 3 mana), plus the Labyrinth already imprinting a card for double colorless, they could potentially cast Sire of Seven Deaths or Devourer of Destiny in upcoming turns with just one more land. Having three copies of Devourer of Destiny is redundant — they only need one to cast and the others are dead cards. Sire of Seven Deaths is arguably the most impactful single threat in their hand with its combination of keywords and lifelink, and it's harder to replace than a third copy of Devourer. A Kozilek's Return would also be a reasonable discard since the opponent has no significant creatures on board, and Kozilek's Return can be triggered from the graveyard when casting an Eldrazi with mana value 7+, but discarding the unique powerful finisher over a redundant third Devourer copy is a meaningful mistake.",
