      "decision_index": 147,
    },
    {
      "severity": "major",
      "description": "Qwen3 Spike declined to counter Flame of Anor with Metallic Rebuke. Flame of Anor is resolving and the opponent is drawing two cards. At 5 life facing a 6/6 Devourer of Destiny, every card the opponent draws increases the chance of finding removal, burn, or another threat to close the game. Metallic Rebuke with Improvise would be very cheap to cast here — with Lavaspur Boots, Aether Spellbomb, Mox Opal, and two Eldrazi Spawn tokens available to tap for Improvise, the effective cost could be as low as {U}. Letting the opponent draw two cards in this position is extremely dangerous when Qwen3 Spike is at such low life and behind on board.",
      "action_taken": "Declined to counter Flame of Anor with Metallic Rebuke, allowing opponent to draw two cards.",
      "better_line": "Cast Metallic Rebuke (using Improvise to tap artifacts) to counter Flame of Anor, denying the opponent two cards while at a critical 5 life total.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 171,
      "player": "Qwen3 Spike",
      "decision_index": 147,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Playing Eldrazi Temple provides redundant mana when Libby already has enough to cast Ugin, Eye of the Storms. Bojuka Bog would exile the opponent's graveyard, disabling delirium (critical since opponent has Unholy Heat in graveyard and multiple card types for delirium). With delirium active, an Unholy Heat from the top would deal 6 damage to Devourer of Destiny, killing it. Exiling the graveyard protects the key attacker.",
      "action_taken": "Played Eldrazi Temple for extra colorless mana",
      "better_line": "Play Bojuka Bog to exile opponent's graveyard, disabling delirium and protecting Devourer of Destiny from potential 6-damage Unholy Heat. Then cast Ugin, Eye of the Storms with existing mana to exile blockers and close the game.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 175,
      "player": "Llama4 Libby",
      "decision_index": 149,
    },
    {
      "severity": "major",
      "description": "Opponent is at 5 life with a 6/6 Devourer of Destiny on board. Even though opponent has Aether Spellbomb (with blue mana available) and 2 Eldrazi Spawn tokens as chump blockers, not attacking forces nothing and gives the opponent free turns. Attacking forces them to either spend Aether Spellbomb (losing a card and letting you recast Devourer for its exile trigger), sacrifice both Spawn tokens (losing mana sources/blockers), or take 6 damage and die.",
      "action_taken": "Skipped the attack phase entirely with a 6/6 on board against an opponent at 5 life.",
      "better_line": "Attack with Devourer of Destiny. If opponent bounces it with Aether Spellbomb, you can recast it next turn with its exile-on-cast trigger and they've lost their Spellbomb. If they chump with Spawn tokens, they lose valuable resources. If they don't block, they die.",
