    {
      "severity": "moderate",
      "description": "Llama4 Libby discarded Ugin, Eye of the Storms, which is one of their most powerful cards and a potential game-ender. They have Ugin's Labyrinth on the battlefield (which produces CC with an exiled card) plus another Ugin's Labyrinth in hand, two Talismans, Eldrazi Temple, Forest, Stomping Ground, and Commercial District — that's 8 lands/mana sources on board producing potentially 9+ mana. With Ugin's Labyrinth producing CC, Eldrazi Temple producing CC for Eldrazi, and the other sources, casting Ugin (7 mana) was very realistic next turn. Against Qwen3 Spike at 5 life with mostly spawn tokens, Ugin would be devastating — exiling colored permanents on cast and with each colorless spell, plus drawing cards and gaining life. The opponent has very limited board presence. Discarding Ugin over a card like Forest, Bojuka Bog, or even the second Ugin's Labyrinth (since one is already on the battlefield and it's legendary) was a significant strategic error.",
