    {
      "severity": "major",
      "description": "Emrakul, the Promised End is on the stack. This is one of the most devastating spells in Magic - when it resolves, Llama4 Libby will gain control of Qwen3 Spike's next turn, meaning they can use Qwen3 Spike's resources to destroy their own board, waste their hand, and set up a losing position. Qwen3 Spike has Metallic Rebuke available with plenty of artifacts to improvise (Mox Opal, Lavaspur Boots, Aether Spellbomb, 2 Eldrazi Spawn tokens = 5 artifacts), meaning they could cast Metallic Rebuke for just {U} by tapping one artifact. The opponent at 9 life with a tapped Devourer of Destiny would need to pay {3} to prevent the counter, and given they likely tapped most of their mana to cast Emrakul, they almost certainly cannot pay. Declining to counter Emrakul here is game-losing.",
      "action_taken": "Declined to counter Emrakul, the Promised End with Metallic Rebuke, allowing it to resolve.",
