    },
    {
      "severity": "major",
      "description": "Emrakul, the Promised End is on the stack. This is one of the most devastating spells in Magic - when it resolves, Llama4 Libby will gain control of Qwen3 Spike's next turn, likely using it to destroy Qwen3 Spike's board and position. Qwen3 Spike has Metallic Rebuke available and has artifacts to improvise with (Mox Opal, Lavaspur Boots, Aether Spellbomb, two Eldrazi Spawn tokens). Metallic Rebuke costs {2}{U} but with improvise, tapping artifacts covers the generic mana. The opponent would need to pay {3} to counter the Rebuke, and with most of their mana likely tapped from casting Emrakul (even with cost reduction), they probably can't pay. Declining to counter Emrakul is game-losing - at 5 life with a minimal board, having the opponent control your turn is almost certainly fatal.",
